 The Xcode project includes native XCTest smoke tests; the Debug/XCTest commands above have not been verified in this preparation. The 2 October unsigned Xcode Release Store build and all 73 registered standalone Release suites pass; see [QA_RESULTS.md](QA_RESULTS.md) for results and blocked signed-runtime checks. Receipts record per-suite results and source fingerprints. Build, tests and the Xcode project use the same source inventory. See [ARCHITECTURE.md](ARCHITECTURE.md) for ownership and module boundaries.
 
+`scripts/project_inventory.py` discovers Swift sources recursively within `Sources/DaBin` for portable builds, QA and Xcode generation. New collaborators live in `State/`, `Storage/`, `Interface/Workspace/` and `Interface/Tutorial/`; existing flat entry points and facades retain their paths. All compile as one Swift module. Source filenames must be unique across these directories, including case variants, and registered resources must have unique filenames because bundles flatten their paths. Nested edits and additions participate in source fingerprints and invalidate cached QA modules.
+
+After source or flat `Tests/*.swift` inventory changes, regenerate with `python3 scripts/generate_project.py` and verify with `python3 scripts/generate_project.py --check`. New standalone Swift suites also need registration in `scripts/run_qa.py`; XCTest builds only `XcodeSmokeTests.swift`. `python3 -B -m unittest discover -s Tests -p 'test_project_inventory.py'` checks nested source discovery, build/QA fingerprints, filename collisions and generated-project parity using temporary fixtures, without compiling Swift or launching the app.
+
 Desktop/Documents synchronization on this Mac reattaches Finder metadata to app bundles, which fails strict signature verification. Use the installed personal-Applications copy; its signature remains verified. The ZIP contains the clean signed file contents, without those extended attributes. `install_app.py` copies a build into personal Applications and verifies it there.
 
